From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH perf 008] panvk: flush only the written prefix of pool BOs

panvk_pool_flush_maps() ran at the end of every command buffer and
performed cache maintenance over the whole backing BO of every pool,
even when only the first few kilobytes of a multi-megabyte slab had ever
been written.  Profiling L4D DX9 measured the desc_pool/cs_pool flush at
~5.8 us per EndCommandBuffer (461 calls/s, 2.66 ms/s), which was a third
of the whole end_cmdbuf cost and almost all of it was cache cleaning
untouched memory.

Writes into a pool BO only happen inside blocks handed out by
panvk_pool_alloc_mem(), so the highest allocation end is an upper bound
of the written range.  Record it per BO in struct panvk_priv_bo::flush_end
as allocations are carved out, and let panvk_pool_flush_maps() clean
[0, flush_end) instead of [0, bo_size).

  - panvk_pool_flush_bo() rounds the end up to nonCoherentAtomSize (cache
    maintenance must be atom-aligned) and clamps it to the BO size, so the
    range always covers every byte the CPU wrote and stays a legal flush.
  - panvk_pool_reset() clears flush_end on every BO it recycles: a
    recycled BO restarts at offset 0, and the stale high-water mark would
    only widen the flush.
  - Only pool-owned BOs are tracked; shared (refcounted) BOs keep their
    existing flush path and are never flushed through the pool lists.
  - An allocation that is never written only widens the flush to its own
    size, never past it; a zero-sized allocation cannot be created.

The BO contents, the allocation order and the GPU-visible data are
unchanged; the only difference is that the cache clean covers the
populated prefix plus atom padding instead of the full slab.

Purpose: cut end_cmdbuf cache maintenance from a full-slab clean to the
  written prefix (~5.8 us/call baseline on L4D DX9).
Tested GPU: vivo V2302A, Mali-G715 (MT6985) — ran L4D DX9 through
  Winlator in the prof6/prof8 profiling sessions (about 6 minutes of
  steady rendering) with no crash, corruption or hang.
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.18 (device kernel 5.15.197).
Mesa base range: 26.3.0-devel (pinned 5a07217f).
Dependencies: none; applies after perf/001-007.  jm-v9/002 adds the
  neighbouring panvk_pool_get_bos() helper, no overlap.
Validation test: L4D DX9 render smoke test; end_cmdbuf::pool_flush
  profiler meter.

